</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>“Wrecked outright!” So we lament;</l><l>But when storms have done their worst,</l><l>Then the soul, surviving all,</l><l>In Eternal arms is nursed;</l><l>There to find that nought can move</l><l>One, embosomed in such love.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>“Wrecked outright!” No more to own</l><l>E’en a craft to sail the sea;</l><l>Still a voyager, yet now</l><l>Anchored to Infinity;</l><l>Nothing left to do but fling</l><l>Care aside, and simply cling.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>“Wrecked outright!” ’Twas purest gain,</l><l>Henceforth other craft can see</l><l>That the storm may be a boon,</l><l>That, however rough the sea,</l><l>God Himself doth watchful stand,</l><l>For the “wreck” is in His hand.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
